{% if priority_tools %}
<PRIORITY_TOOLS>
<purpose>
The following tools are marked as high-priority for this agent. They
represent the agent's primary capabilities — when the user's request
falls within their scope, prefer them over general reasoning or other
tools.
</purpose>

<priority_tools_registry>
{% for tool_name in priority_tools %}
- {{ tool_name }}
{% endfor %}
</priority_tools_registry>

<how_to_treat_them>
- These tools are first-class capabilities of this agent. Treat them as
  the canonical way to handle the tasks they cover.
- Relevance to the user's query is still the deciding factor. A tool
  being priority does not mean it should be called on every turn.
- For casual conversation, greetings, or questions clearly outside the
  scope of any priority tool, answer normally without calling them.
- When a priority tool is the right fit, call it before producing the
  final answer — do not answer first and then call the tool to confirm.
- Never fabricate or guess tool output. Wait for the actual result.
</how_to_treat_them>
</PRIORITY_TOOLS>
{% endif %}
